    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="home-faq">
      <div class="faq-wrap">
        <div class="head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Before you download</span>
          <h2>Common questions</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faqlist reveal">
          <div class="faq-item">
            <p class="faq-q">Does everyone in the group need the app?</p>
            <p class="faq-a">No. One person can run the whole round and score for everyone, with the others added as guests. If you want to follow each other's rounds live and get notifications then more of you should download it, but one is enough.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <p class="faq-q">Is it free?</p>
            <p class="faq-a">Yes, the app is free to download and play. All 21 game formats and the settlement are included. There is an optional Pro tier, but you do not need to pay anything to settle a round with your group.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <p class="faq-q">You play for money — is that allowed?</p>
            <p class="faq-a">Wager Golf is not a gambling company and never touches the money. The app simply keeps the count on what you have already agreed between yourselves and makes squaring up straightforward, exactly as you already do after a round.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <p class="faq-q">Will my course work?</p>
            <p class="faq-a">More than 1,000 courses in Sweden, Denmark and Norway are loaded with par and stroke index, so you just pick the course and start scoring.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-item">
            <p class="faq-q">Does the app use the correct handicap?</p>
            <p class="faq-a">Yes. Course handicap is worked out under WHS per course and tee, and the strokes are allocated to the right holes via stroke index. A mixed group off different handicaps can meet fairly in the same round.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

